# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored — never commit real values.
#
# ⚠️  IMPORTANT — what this does and does not protect
#
# Expo inlines every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable into the JavaScript bundle at build
# time. Anyone with the APK can extract these values. Using a .env file keeps
# secrets out of version control; it does NOT make them secret in a shipped app.
#
# Consequences:
#   * The GCS service account MUST be scoped to the single backup bucket
#     (roles/storage.objectAdmin on that bucket only — never project-wide), so a
#     leaked key can't reach anything else. Rotate it if the APK is shared.
#   * For the Anthropic key, prefer leaving it blank here and entering it in-app
#     (Settings → AI program generation). In-app keys live in the app's private
#     database instead of the bundle, so they are not in the APK at all. The only
#     way to truly keep an API key off the device is to call it through a backend
#     you control.
#
# See docs/cloud-sync-setup.md for the full setup and rotation steps.

# --- Google Cloud Storage backup ---
# Bucket name only, no gs:// prefix.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GCS_BUCKET=

# The service account JSON key, compacted onto ONE line and wrapped in SINGLE
# quotes. Single quotes matter: they stop dotenv from expanding the \n escapes
# inside private_key, which must survive verbatim for JSON.parse.
#   node -e "console.log(JSON.stringify(require('./key.json')))"
EXPO_PUBLIC_GCS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# --- Anthropic API (AI program generation) ---
# Recommended: leave blank and enter the key in-app instead (see note above).
EXPO_PUBLIC_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
